course: dictionary
lesson: 2910
title: Downwards: lower and smaller
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Downwards means towards a lower place or position. «Gravity is the pull of the Earth that makes things fall downwards.» Things fall down, towards the ground, so downwards points to the lower place.
explain: Downwards can also mean going to a smaller number or amount. Count downwards from ten and you say 9, 8, 7, and so on. Each number is smaller than the one before.
explain: Look at the words around downwards to check which meaning fits. «A plane's wings push air downwards, and the air pushes the plane upwards.» Here the air moves to a lower place, and the pairing with upwards shows the direction clearly.
explain: Downwards is the adverb. Downward is the adjective, used before a noun, as in a downward slope. Both are close in meaning, so you can use either one in a sentence about direction.
fact: Downwards means towards a lower place or position.
fact: Downwards can also mean going to a smaller number or amount.
fact: Upwards is the opposite of downwards.
fact: «Gravity is the pull of the Earth that makes things fall downwards.»
fact: Downward is the adjective: a downward slope goes towards a lower place.
exercise: «Gravity is the pull of the Earth that makes things fall downwards.» Which way do things fall? | *Downwards, towards the ground | Round and round | Upwards | Sideways
exercise: When you count downwards from ten, which numbers do you say? | 1, 2, 3 | 11, 12, 13 | 10, 20, 30 | *9, 8, 7
exercise: Which word means the opposite of upwards? | Forwards | Inside | *Downwards | Round
test: «A plane's wings push air downwards, and the air pushes the plane upwards.» Which way does the air move? | *Downwards | Upwards | Backwards | Not at all
test: When a graph slopes downwards, what happens to the numbers as you move along it? | Missing | The same | Bigger | *Smaller
exam: In «count downwards from ten», what happens to the numbers? | They turn into words | They stay the same | They get bigger | *They get smaller
